+Issue #2: Setup Express.js server and create GET /todos endpoint
+Details:
+Initialize a Node.js and Express.js backend project for a To-Do application and implement the endpoint to fetch all to-dos.
+
+Requirements:
+- Create `package.json` with `express` and `cors` dependencies, and add a `"start": "node index.js"` script.
+- Create `index.js` that sets up an Express server running on port `3000` (or `process.env.PORT`).
+- Create an in-memory array `todos` pre-populated with 2 sample to-do items so the API returns sample data right away. Each to-do object should have `id`, `title`, and `completed` (boolean) fields.
+- Create a `GET /todos` endpoint that returns HTTP status 200 and the JSON list of all `todos`.
+- Add a clear `README.md` file mentioning that this is an Express.js To-Do REST API and explaining how to run it.
+

